<apex:page showHeader="false" sidebar="false" standardStylesheets="false"
           applyHtmlTag="false" applyBodyTag="false" docType="html-5.0"
           title="Privacy | Curb Cut" cache="true" expires="300">
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8"/>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/>
  <meta name="description" content="What Curb Cut collects, what deliberately does not exist in the system, and who processes it."/>
  <title>Privacy | Curb Cut</title>
</head>
<body>
<c:CurbCutShell pageTitle="Privacy" current="privacy"
  eyebrow="Privacy Policy, updated 30 August 2026"
  heading="What we hold, and what does not exist."
  lede="The safest way to protect something is not to collect it. Most of this is about what there is nowhere to put.">

  <section>
    <div class="plain">
      <span class="tag">The short version</span>
      <p>
        We keep a scrambled version of your phone number, what you tell us is
        hard at work, and anything you ask us to remember. There is no field for
        a diagnosis, so we could not store one if we tried.
      </p>
      <p>
        We never sell it, never share it for anyone else's purposes, and never
        use it to advertise to you. You can see what is held, turn it off, or
        have it deleted, at any time, without giving a reason.
      </p>
      <p>The rest of this page says the same thing more carefully.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What does not exist here</h2>
    <div class="note absent">
      <p>
        There is no field anywhere in this system for a <strong>diagnosis</strong>,
        <strong>condition</strong>, <strong>disability type</strong>,
        <strong>medical note</strong>, <strong>severity</strong> or
        <strong>prognosis</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Not hidden, not locked, not encrypted &mdash; absent. If you mention a
        condition anyway, it is not written to any record, and you are told so in
        the same reply. An automated check refuses to let the software be built
        if anyone ever adds such a field.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What we do keep</h2>
    <table class="facts">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">A scrambled phone number</th>
          <td>So your conversation carries on across messages. Your number is
              turned into an irreversible code the moment it arrives. The number
              itself is never saved and never written to a log.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">What you say is hard</th>
          <td>In your own words, so we can look up what might help. What is
              difficult, never why it is difficult.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Anything you ask us to remember</th>
          <td>A standing preference, in your exact words, and who you chose to
              let see it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Requests you approved</th>
          <td>So the request you agreed to can be sent, and so you can see what
              came back.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Every time a preference was shown</th>
          <td>So you can see it. Something that travels ahead of you into a new
              team is a disclosure made while you were not in the room. You are
              entitled to know it happened.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Conversations are anonymous unless you choose otherwise.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What we never do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>We never sell your information.</strong> Not to anyone, at any
          price.</li>
      <li><strong>We never hand it to anyone for their own purposes.</strong>
          No data brokers, no advertisers, no analytics companies.</li>
      <li><strong>We never advertise to you.</strong> No promotional messages are
          sent at all. Every message you get is a reply to one you sent.</li>
      <li><strong>We never guess things about you.</strong> Nothing is profiled
          or predicted from your behaviour. Every signal in the system is one you
          set yourself, in your own words.</li>
      <li><strong>We never tell your employer anything you did not approve</strong>,
          in the conversation, at the time.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who else touches it</h2>
    <p>
      Two companies handle data so the service can work at all. Neither may use
      it for their own ends.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Twilio</strong> carries the messages and calls, and necessarily
          handles your phone number to deliver them, as any phone company must.</li>
      <li><strong>Salesforce</strong> hosts the database and the assistant.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Information is stored on Salesforce infrastructure in the United States. We
      give it to no one else, except where the law compels it &mdash; and there is
      no medical information in the system to give.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What you can do, any time</h2>
    <ul class="kwlist">
      <li><span class="kw">WHO</span><span>See everyone who has been shown a preference of yours.</span></li>
      <li><span class="kw">OFF</span><span>Turn a saved preference off. Immediate. You will not be asked why &mdash; there is nowhere to record a reason, so nobody can ask you for one later.</span></li>
      <li><span class="kw">DELETE</span><span>Throw away a drafted request before it is sent.</span></li>
      <li><span class="kw">STOP</span><span>Stop receiving messages from the number entirely.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Or email <a href="mailto:parth.sevak2@gmail.com">parth.sevak2@gmail.com</a>
      to ask what is held about you, correct it, or have it deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      Records are kept only while the request or preference they belong to is
      live. An anonymous conversation that leads nowhere leaves nothing behind
      that could identify you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If this changes</h2>
    <p>
      A changed policy appears here with a new date at the top. Carrying on using
      the service after that means the newer version applies.
    </p>
  </section>

</c:CurbCutShell>
</body>
</html>
</apex:page>
